Subject: [PATCH] B3a v2 gate, run once on seeds 4001-5000: NOT MET

S1 coverage 0.890 (bar >= 0.90), S2 median 95% region 26.1% of the domain (bar <= 25%), S3 median
centroid error 1.45 x the station spacing (bar <= 0.5 x): NOT MET on all three; 34 sessions not
located (V7, counted against the method) and 379 redraws. S4 read for platforms only (V12): the
recorded rows reproduce bit for bit in debug against the release build here, and the new ci.yml
job b3a-v2-determinism runs the same test on Linux, macOS and Windows; the CLI, Python and
WebAssembly half is not assessable in 0.41. oracle.py's v2 mode agrees with the engine on gate-input
seeds 4001-4020, run after the gate (V15).

RESULTS-v2.md records the gate, the development numbers seen before it (S1 0.905, S2 0.288,
S3 1.50), v1 against v2, and descriptive splits after the run (located only: 0.921 / 0.251 / 1.40;
inside the hull: 0.925 / 0.208 / 1.05). tests/locator_power_difference_v2.rs pins the miss and
reproduces 12 recorded rows. gate-v2.json.gz holds every row. The row stops: no real run on
Jammertest 2027 with this method, and v1 stays published.
